We at PNG Air pride ourselves as the leading domestic airline operating over 26 ports across the length and breadth of Papua New Guinea as the carrier of choice. Operating the largest fleet of ATR 72-600 series in the region. We are committed to providing affordable world class experience addressing competitive passenger fare regimes and cargo charges ensuring reliable and safe on time services to our valued customers and stakeholders.


AIRPORT MANAGER (Tari
)


The Airport Department is seeking suitably qualified local based applicants to apply for its Airport Manager role, based in Tari.  


Reporting to the Regional Airport Manager; this position will be responsible for the following accountabilities:




Manage all aspects of the Operations to ensure 100% OTP in all turn around;


Provide overall management, leadership and support to all staff;


Develop and implement cost efficient methods to assist the port operations;


Monitor and manage all expenses within approved budget;


Overall management of GSE in the allocated airport;


Provide support to NAC and all other stakeholders;


Identify and improve RPT scheduling issues affecting operations;


Provide feedback to appropriate departments;


Participate in inspections and audits, liaise with regulators and report where required;


Ensure Safety at work is adhered too;


Schedule and facilitate emergency and table top exercises;


Investigate and solve local port issues.




Qualifications, Skills and Competencies:




Tertiary Qualification-Diploma in Business Management or equivalent


Previous Managerial experience in the Airline Industry is preferable


Excellent Reporting, interpersonal and communication skills.


Ability to work independently and manage multiple priorities.


Must have good written and verbal communication skills.


Must be presentable and have good hygiene.


Must have a valid PNG Driver’s license and Police Clearance







